mt7996: bypass broken SDO TX path on MT7990

The connac3 SDO (Software Defined Offload) firmware path fills TX
descriptors for normal 802.3 unicast data frames. On MT7990 this
firmware path is broken: TX rate descriptor fields are malformed,
clamping AP transmit at 6 Mbit/s even with a perfect link. Result:
AP->client (download) collapses to ~92 Mbit/s while client->AP
(upload) runs at line rate.

The driver already recognizes that MT7990 lacks the WA workaround
component used by MT7996/MT7992 (mt7996_has_wa returns !is_mt7990),
so this extends the existing guard so MT7990 always fills the TXD
from the host (matches pre-SDO behavior, commit 325a0c49).
MT7996/MT7992 retain SDO unchanged.

References: openwrt/mt76 #1043, #1065; commit 55218e63 (re-enabled SDO).

diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
index 7d454e21..fd19a461 100644
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1094,7 +1094,7 @@ int mt7996_tx_prepare_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, void *txwi_ptr,
 	pid = mt76_tx_status_skb_add(mdev, wcid, tx_info->skb);
 	memset(txwi_ptr, 0, MT_TXD_SIZE);
 	/* Transmit non qos data by 802.11 header and need to fill txd by host*/
-	if (!is_8023 || pid >= MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST)
+	if (!is_8023 || pid >= MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST || is_mt7990(&dev->mt76))
 		mt7996_mac_write_txwi(dev, txwi_ptr, tx_info->skb, wcid, key,
 				      pid, qid, 0);
 
@@ -1146,7 +1146,7 @@ int mt7996_tx_prepare_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, void *txwi_ptr,
 
 		txp->fw.flags = cpu_to_le16(MT_CT_INFO_FROM_HOST);
 
-		if (!is_8023 || pid >= MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST)
+		if (!is_8023 || pid >= MT_PACKET_ID_FIRST || is_mt7990(&dev->mt76))
 			txp->fw.flags |= cpu_to_le16(MT_CT_INFO_APPLY_TXD);
 
 		if (!key)
